# Start program: run the real robot's program through the twin (ADR-0071).
#
# Per cycle, in the order `python3 -m cite_bringup.program` uses: a work-piece
# on every simulated side's pick table and that side's belt running; on a pair
# with a physical side, the twin's mode READ as SIM, the physical carriage
# checked, and the operator's ConfirmPart awaited; the arm's custody read;
# VALIDATED; one cycle of the program; and, with a physical side, SIM again.
# Rejected unless Start robot has succeeded and the console is READY. A failed
# step ends the run and leaves the console in FAULT; nothing is retried and
# nothing homes. Cancelling the goal is the same software stop as StopCell.
#
# Served under `/cite/<zone>/console/<NAME>` (ConsoleState.msg).

string NAME="run_program"

float64 speed_scale     # (0, 1] of the program's own speed, sent explicitly by
                        # the operator's panel. Never defaulted: a goal with 0, or
                        # any value outside (0, 1], is rejected (ADR-0071 decision 2)
uint32 cycles           # how many cycles, at least 1. 0 is REJECTED rather than
                        # read as "until stopped": a run with no end is asked for
                        # by number, never by leaving a field unset
---
bool success
string detail           # what was done, or which step failed and why
uint32 cycles_completed # cycles that ran every step to the end
---
uint32 cycle            # 1-based number of the cycle in progress
uint32 step_index       # 1-based number of the step in progress within it
uint32 step_count       # how many steps one cycle has
string step             # the step in progress, as the operator reads it
